<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rao Chhatrasal of Bundi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1658</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rao <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhatrasal">Chhatrasal</a> was the Hada <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhan</a> ruler of Bundi in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> from 1631 to 1658. A commander in Mughal service, he fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> and the north-west. In the war of succession among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a>'s sons he took the side of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dara-shikoh">Dara Shikoh</a> and was killed fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-samugarh">Battle of Samugarh</a> in 1658.</p></div>
